 end of chapter 3 this is  the very book that we'll be focusing on  in this video there have been tons of  questions and rumors on what this  mysterious fairy tale could be well some  signs point to Aladdin while others  point to Sleeping Beauty and we're about  to tell you why signs that point to  Aladdin for starters we can definitely  check off the part about far-off places  daring sword fights and magic spells  Ruba totally counts as a far-off place  and we don't have a shortage of  swordfights either in regards to magic  genie in the magic carpet would  definitely count as magical creatures to  give you guys a little recap on the  prince in disguise  Aladdin once asked the genie to grant  him a wish in order to win over Princess  Jasmine with his lavish lifestyle and  all of his riches signs that point to  Sleeping Beauty as for the idea that  Belle is reading the Sleeping Beauty  book there's also a ton of clues as to  why this is also a pretty solid theory  we've got the far-off place down pat  since this classic takes place once upon  a time in a land far far away we also  definitely see a sword fight take place  between Prince Phillip and Maleficent  this story pretty much revolves around  magic spells as well  from the wicked spell placed on Aurora  to all the magic that the three fairies  flora fauna and Merryweather bring to  the tables  finally our prince in disguise makes an  appearance as Prince Phillip dancing  with Aurora in the middle of the woods  she in fact does not discover that it's  him until the very end of this story  we guess now there is nothing left to do  but to compare these two storylines do  you guys think that the book that Belle  is so interested in is Aladdin  or do you think it could be Sleeping  Beauty for Aladdin we're going to need  you to come in a red heart down below  with the hashtag Aladdin for Sleeping  Beauty go ahead and leave a blue heart  so for those of you who voted for  Sleeping Beauty this totally makes sense  since we do get a glimpse into the page  that Belle is reading oddly the picture  we see looks like something straight out  of Sleeping Beauty we see a forest and a  great castle in the background which we  have to admit looks nothing like Agrabah  on the other hand Disney is known for  hinting at movies to come and they do  this by releasing Easter eggs in their  newest films this could definitely be  the case with these two movies since  Aladdin was released just a year after  Beauty and the bees there's also the  fact that Princess Jasmine doesn't  actually realize that it's Aladdin  dressed as Prince ollie until later on  in the story maybe even somewhere near  chapter 3 so with both of these theories  looking pretty solid right now and a ton  of facts to support them both it took a  whole lot of internet digging to come up  with a conclusion the answer did this  Disney theory lies in the most magical  place on earth Disneyland  believe it or not that some dedicated  fans went to Disneyland to ask Belle  this very question and according to  multiple sources if you were to actually  ask Belle what book she was reading she  would let you know that the book was in  fact Sleeping Beauty there's also a  cottage in the Disneyland parks that  represents where Belle grew up in the  middle of this cottage you'll come  across the book Sleeping Beauty and it  said that Belle's mother used to read it  to her as a child so we guess that the  undeniable winner of this Disney theory  battle is in fact Sleeping Beauty be  sure to share this video with all of  your friends to find out if you were on  the same side of this did the theory  battle this is actually pretty cool  since you can definitely tell that Belle  has been inspired by Princess Aurora  from Sleeping Beauty in more ways than  just one  they are both known to be romantic  gentle and caring princesses who always  carry themselves with grace so did you  guess correctly let us know in the  comments section below and wh